  "query_preview": "/Through Wednesday/...\nIssued at 304 AM MDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nA weak upper level trough will move across the area today into this \nevening.  Considerable monsoon moisture will remain over the area \nwith PW's from 150% to 200% above normal. Thus will see another \nround of showers and storms across much of the area, with areas \nof heavy rainfall, in some places. Flow aloft will increase \ntoday, so storm movements will be faster than the previous two \ndays. Meanwhile SBCAPE will range of 1500 to 2000 j/kg over the \nplains. Shear is a little better this aftn, however, mid level \ntemps are very warm. Thus, main threat from stronger storms would \nbe wet microbursts similar to what occurred last evening. As far \nas highs, readings will be in the mid 80s to lower 90's across the\nplains.\n\nFor tonight, the weak upper level trough will move to the east with \nshower and tstm activity gradually ending across the plains by mid \nto late evening. \n\nLooking ahead to Fri and Sat, the upper level high will gradually \nbuild back into the area with a decrease in monsoon moisture. \nHowever, there will still be some residual moisture, for sct tstms \nin the mtns, especially on Sat. Across the plains, it will be mainly \ndry with highs reaching the upper 90's to lower 100's on Sat. \n\nFor Sun thru next Tue, an upper level high will extend from the \nGreat Basin across Colorado.  Both the ECMWF and GFS show an \nincrease in monsoon moisture.  Thus will see an increasing chc for \nshowers and storms over the higher terrain and across the plains for \nMon and Tue.  Temperatures will continue hot over nern CO Sun and \nMon.  By Mon night into Tue a weak cool front may move across which \nwould allow for highs to drop back to more seasonal levels.",
